{"id":"leaning-tower-of-pisa","name":"Leaning Tower of Pisa","qid":"Q39054","country":"Italy","locality":"Pisa","lat":"43.72301","lon":"10.396624","built":"1173","year":1173,"year_text":"1173","century":"12th century","era":"Middle Ages","period":"","date_basis":"Wikidata, inception","style":"Romanesque architecture","heritage":"Italian national heritage; part of UNESCO World Heritage Site","type":"inclined tower; church tower","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leaning_Tower_of_Pisa","text":"The Leaning Tower of Pisa (Italian: torre pendente di Pisa [ˈtorre penˈdɛnte di ˈpiːza, - ˈpiːsa]), or simply the Tower of Pisa (torre di Pisa), is the campanile, or freestanding bell tower, of Pisa Cathedral. It is known for its nearly four-degree lean, the result of an unstable foundation. The tower is one of three structures in Pisa's Cathedral Square (Piazza del Duomo), which includes the cathedral and Pisa Baptistry.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leaning_Tower_of_Pisa","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[{"id":"gh-28616d77b229","w":900,"h":1200,"title":"2017-06-21 Pisa 14.jpg","o":"gh-28616d77b229.jpg","credit":{"text":"Nemo bis","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2017-06-21_Pisa_14.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-720bfececd81","w":800,"h":1200,"title":"Pisa by night - panoramio (1).jpg","o":"gh-720bfececd81.jpg","credit":{"text":"Nikolai Karaneschev","license":"CC BY 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pisa_by_night_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-7a114fae41ea","w":541,"h":1200,"title":"Campanile Dôme - Pise (IT52) - 2022-08-31 - 20.jpg","o":"gh-7a114fae41ea.jpg","credit":{"text":"Chabe01","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:C